  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_unique_value:r7:t6",
    "narration": "Iris was quiet for a long breath after the question. Her gaze moved across the bare floorboards, then to the empty cabinets against the far wall, as though the sparse room might offer her something to work with.\n\n\"I don't know yet,\" she said. The words came without apology or softening — just plain, the way someone states a fact about the weather. \"I haven't been here long enough to know where my lines are with you. Or with anyone.\"\n\nShe paused, and her thumb brushed once across the knuckles of her other hand. When she spoke again her voice had not changed in tone, but it was slower, more deliberate. \"Ask me again later. When I've seen enough of how you handle things to answer it honestly.\"",
